ory for numbers (attention/accuracy). So we can bring up that concern. Also we have no info on crew cooperation beyond remarks. So we can say we agree with B's strengths but note the weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks may affect crew cooperation and attention. Suggest we need more info on B's crew cooperation. Also we could bring up Candidate D's strengths as alternative. But we need to keep focused. Perhaps we can say we still support B but want to probe B's communication and numeric memory. Or we could shift to Candidate D if we think concerns outweigh B's strengths. Let's evaluate: B's weak memory for numbers could be critical for flight operations (e.g., fuel calculations). That is a serious concern. Combined with nasty remarks, may affect crew. So maybe we should reconsider. Candidate D has strong responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but has hot temper and know-it-all. But no mention of numeric memory issues. D's hot temper could affect crew. Which is worse? Numeric memory is safety-critical. So maybe D is better overall. But we need to discuss. We could propose shifting to D as alternative, citing D's strengths and noting that while D has hot temper, we haven't seen evidence of communication issues beyond that. So we could say we think D may be a stronger overall fit. Let's decide: I think we should challenge B's lead, propose D as stronger alternative, citing D's concentration, problem solving, responsibility, and note that hot temper is a concern but may be manageable. Also note D's ability to respond to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience). So we can shift vote to D. Provide reasoning. Also ask others for info on D's crew cooperation. So our vote: Candidate D.\n\nThus public message: I disagree with B being the best; while B's reliability and stress handling are good, the weak numeric memory and nasty remarks raise serious concerns for safety and crew cooperation. Candidate D shows strong concentration, problem solving, respons